s any subsidy, address subsidies, address subsidy, address the subsidies, address the subsidy, addressed all subsidies, addressed all subsidy, addressed any subsidies, addressed any subsidy, addressed subsidies, addressed subsidy, addressed the subsidies, addressed the subsidy, addresses all subsidies, addresses all subsidy, addresses any subsidies, addresses any subsidy, addresses subsidies, addresses subsidy, addresses the subsidies, addresses the subsidy, addressing all subsidies, addressing all subsidy, addressing any subsidies, addressing any subsidy, addressing subsidies, addressing subsidy, addressing the subsidies, addressing the subsidy, eliminate all subsidies, eliminate all subsidy, eliminate any subsidies, eliminate any subsidy, eliminates all subsidies, eliminates all subsidy, eliminates any subsidies, eliminates any subsidy, eliminates subsidies, eliminates subsidy, eliminates the subsidies, eliminates the subsidy, eliminating all subsidies, eliminating all subsidy, eliminating any subsidies, eliminating any subsidy, end all subsidies, end all subsidy, end any subsidies, end any subsidy, end subsidies, end subsidy, end the subsidies, end the subsidy, ending all subsidies, ending all subsidy, ending any subsidies, ending any subsidy, ending subsidies, ending subsidy, ending the subsidies, ending the subsidy, ends all subsidies, ends all subsidy, ends any subsidies, ends any subsidy, ends subsidies, ends subsidy, ends the subsidies, ends the subsidy, phase-out all subsidies, phase-out all subsidy, phase-out any subsidies, phase-out any subsidy, phase-out subsidies, phase-out subsidy, phase-out the subsidies, phase-out the subsidy, phases out all subsidies, phases out all subsidy, phases out any subsidies, phases out any subsidy, phases out subsidies, phases out subsidy, phases out the subsidies, phases out the subsidy, phasing out all subsidies, phasing out all subsidy, phasing out any subsidies, phasing out any subsidy, reform all subsidies, reform all subsidy, reform any subsidies, reform any subsidy, reform subsidies, reform subsidy, reform the subsidies, reform the subsidy, reforming all subsidies, reforming all subsidy, reforming any subsidies, reforming any subsidy, reforms all subsidies, reforms all subsidy, reforms any subsidies, reforms any subsidy, reforms subsidies, reforms subsidy, reforms the subsidies, reforms the subsidy, remove all subsidies, remove all subsidy, remove any subsidies, remove any subsidy, remove subsidies, remove subsidy, remove the subsidies, remove the subsidy, removes all subsidies, removes all subsidy, removes any subsidies, removes any subsidy, removes subsidies, removes subsidy, removes the subsidies, removes the subsidy, removing all subsidies, removing all subsidy, removing any subsidies, removing any subsidy, subsidies are eliminated, subsidies are ended, subsidies are removed, subsidies phase-out, subsidies should be eliminated, subsidies will be eliminated, subsidies will be removed, subsidy are eliminated, subsidy are ended, subsidy are removed, subsidy phase-out, subsidy should be eliminated, subsidy will be eliminated, subsidy will be removed</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">6kf4hg59</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1274"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Removing subsidies can help reduce costs, better align economic incentives with environmental goals, and promote equity. This can mitigate environmental harm and discourage harmful behaviour. However, it may also end support for renewable energy development or negatively impact communities, households, and businesses.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Removing subsidies can help reduce costs, better align economic incentives with environmental goals, and promote equity. This can mitigate environmental harm and discourage harmful behaviour. However, it may also end support for renewable energy development or negatively impact communities, households, and businesses.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1276 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1276">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q722"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">direct investment</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">direct investments, public capital expenditure, public investment, public investments</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1554"/>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2407"/>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">dp92w33k</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1554"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Direct investments by the governments using public funds. This can be to support climate initiatives or integrate climate into other projects or investing in research and development to develop new technologies and reduce the cost of climate change solutions.</cpr:P7>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">FDI</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">foreign direct investment</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">foreign direct investments</cpr:P9>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Direct investments by the governments using public funds. This can be to support climate initiatives or integrate climate into other projects.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1277 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1277">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q722"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fees and charges</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">fee and charge, fee and charges, fees and charge</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">smhdpm2v</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Compulsory, required payments to the government that are levied more-or-less in proportion to the services provided. Fees and charges range from entrance fees to national parks, charges on land-based sewage discharge.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Compulsory, required payments to the government that are levied more-or-less in proportion to the services provided. Fees and charges range from entrance fees to national parks, charges on land-based sewage discharge.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1278 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1278">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q722"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">insurance</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">risk underwriting, insured, insurance program, insurance programmes, insurance programs</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2403"/>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">k9vkk2p7</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1580"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Financial support to help individuals manage the effects of unexpected events, securing their livelihoods and increasing the resilience of people and businesses to the changing climate. It’s especially vital in developing regions where everyday risks, climate-related weather extremes, or crop failures can push people into poverty. Without insurance, people may have to resort to selling assets or cutting consumption to cope with losses.</cpr:P7>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">export credit insurance</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">health insurance</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">insurance and reinsurance undertakings</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">liability insurance</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">life insurance</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">medical insurance</cpr:P9>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Financial support to help individuals manage the effects of unexpected events, securing their livelihoods and increasing the resilience of people and businesses to the changing climate. It’s especially vital in developing regions where everyday risks, climate-related weather extremes, or crop failures can push people into poverty. Without insurance, people may have to resort to selling assets or cutting consumption to cope with losses.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1279 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1279">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q722"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">feed-in-tariff</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">feed-in-tariff, feed in tariff, feed in tariffs, feed-in-tariffs, FIT scheme, FIT schemes, feed-in tariff, feed-in tariff program, feed-in tariffs, FIT program, FIT programme, FIT programmes, FIT programs, FiT, FiT program, FiT programme, FiT programmes, FiT programs, FiT scheme, FiT schemes, Feed in Tariff, Feed-in Tariff, Feed-in Tariffs, feed-in-program, (FiT), (FIT), Feed in tariff, Feed in tariffs, Feed in Tariffs, Feed-in tariff, FEED-IN TARIFF, Feed-in tariffs, Feed-In-Tariff, FEED-IN-TARIFF, Feed-In-Tariffs, FEED-IN-TARIFFS, Feed- in Tariff, feedintariff, feedintariffs</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2405"/>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q715"/>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">5gvxthzq</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q567"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A policy instrument designed to support the development and acceleration of renewable energy sources by providing a guaranteed, above-market price for producers.</cpr:P7>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">FIT FOR 55</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">Fit for 55</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">Fit-for-55</cpr:P9>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A policy instrument designed to support the development and acceleration of renewable energy sources by providing a guaranteed, above-market price for producers.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q128 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q128">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1892"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">artificial reef</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">artificial reefs</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P4 rdf:resource="https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/publication/149400/technologies-climate-change-adaptation.pdf"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Artificial reefs have been constructed from discarded human-made materials, such as tires, concrete blocks, or even old subway cars, in areas of oceans where reefs have been depleted. Organisms such as algae and barnacles then attach to these surfaces and lay the ecological groundwork for a reef to bloom.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1280 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1280">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q722"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tradable permit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">tradable permits, tradable certificate, tradable certificates, tradable credit, tradable credits</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">jbqjz2ve</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Tradable permits are market-based tools that grant permission for specific activities, frequently used to regulate emissions. These permits can be issued within a trading system to manage environmental impacts. Two primary trading systems exist: &quot;cap-and-trade,&quot; which sets an emissions cap for trading allowances, and &quot;baseline-and-credit,&quot; which rewards reductions below a set baseline.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Tradable permits are market-based tools that grant permission for specific activities, frequently used to regulate emissions. These permits can be issued within a trading system to manage environmental impacts.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1281 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1281">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1207"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">codes and standards</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">code and standard, standard and code, standards and codes, eco-design, ecodesign, ESPR, product standard, product standards, technical regulation, technical regulations</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">htggzu76</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Codes and standards are regulatory instruments that specify minimum standards to protect health and safety. This ranges from performance standards, which prescribe outcomes while allowing flexibility to achieve compliance, to the more prescriptive approach of technology-specific standards.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Codes and standards are regulatory instruments that specify minimum standards to protect health and safety. This ranges from performance standards, which prescribe outcomes while allowing flexibility to achieve compliance, to the more prescriptive approach of technology-specific standards.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1282 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1282">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1207"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">zoning and spatial planning</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">spatial planning, zoning, spatial policy, zoning policy, land-use plan, land-use planning, land-use zoning</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">z7cnc9cz</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Zoning and spatial planning are both methods for guiding the distribution of people and activities in a space, and are regulatory restrictions. Zoning helps manage multiple uses within protected areas, such as biodiversity conservation and human development.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Zoning and spatial planning are both methods for guiding the distribution of people and activities in a space, and are regulatory restriction.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1283 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1283">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1207"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">permits and licenses</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">environmental permits and licenses, environmental permits and Licensing</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Environmental permits and licenses regulate business activities that could impact the environment or human health, including climate change. Business activities that may cause pollution or that pose another risk to the environment are regulated.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Environmental permits and licenses regulate business activities that could impact the environment or human health, including climate change.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1284 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1284">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1207"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">due diligence</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">duty of care, duty of vigilance, ESDD, HRDD, HREDD, CS3D, CSDDD, EUDR, vigilance plan</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">v58nzb77</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">The processes through which enterprises can identify, prevent, mitigate and account for how they address their actual and potential adverse impacts. Due diligence is the idea that reasonable precautions should be taken to avoid causing harm to people, the environment, or society. It also involves identifying and mitigating risks before they occur.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">The processes through which enterprises can identify, prevent, mitigate and account for how they address their actual and potential adverse impacts. Due diligence is the idea that reasonable precautions should be taken to avoid causing harm to people, the environment, or society. It also involves identifying and mitigating risks before they occur.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1285 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1285">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1207"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ban</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ban on, banned, banning, prohibition measure, prohibition measures, bans, outlaw, outlawed, outlawing, outlaws, prohibit, prohibited, prohibiting, prohibition, prohibitions, prohibits, forbidden, forbids, no new coal, no new oil and gas, PFAS restriction, REACH restriction, forbid, restriction proposal</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1275"/>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1313"/>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1612"/>
        <cpr:P11 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2406"/>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">s6jbaw6e</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A ban is a legal action that prevents the sale or supply of a product or service, or that recalls a product from the market. Examples are bans on SF6, greenwashing, fossil fuel advertisement or single-use plastics.</cpr:P7>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">cannot forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">did not forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">do not forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">does not forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">nor forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">not expressly forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">not expressly or impliedly forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">not impliedly forbid</cpr:P9>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">ur ban</cpr:P9>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A ban is a legal action that prevents the sale or supply of a product or service, or that recalls a product from the market. Examples are bans on SF6, greenwashing, fossil fuel advertisement or single-use plastics.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1286 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1286">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1208"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1833"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">early warning system</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">early warning systems, EWS, EWSs, early action system, early action systems, early warning information, early warning and monitoring, early warning and surveillance system, early warning and surveillance systems, early warning, early warning actions, early warning action, early warning alert, early warning alerts</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">er37udyk</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q374"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q769"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q83"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">An integrated system of hazard monitoring, forecasting and prediction, disaster risk assessment, communication and preparedness activities systems and processes that enables individuals, communities, governments, businesses and others to take timely action to reduce disaster risks in advance of hazardous events. To be effective, they need to be end-to-end and people-centred.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">An integrated system of hazard monitoring, forecasting and prediction, that enables individuals, communities, governments, businesses and others to take timely action to reduce disaster risks in advance of hazardous events.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1287 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1287">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1286"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">multi-hazard early warning system</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">MHEWS, multi risk early warning system, multi risk early warning systems, multi-risk early warning system, multi-risk early warning systems, multi hazard EWS, multi-hazard EWS</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q83"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A multi-hazard early warning system is an integrated system which allows people to know that hazardous weather or climate events are on their way, and informs how governments, communities, and individuals can act to minimise it&apos;s impacts. It should include risk knowledge, observation and forecasting, communication, as well as response.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A multi-hazard early warning system is an integrated system which allows people to know that hazardous weather or climate events are on their way, and informs how governments, communities, and individuals can act to minimise it&apos;s impacts.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


