 all fossil fuel subsidy, remove any fossil fuel subsidies, remove any fossil fuel subsidy, remove fossil fuel subsidies, remove fossil fuel subsidy, remove the fossil fuel subsidies, remove the fossil fuel subsidy, removes all fossil fuel subsidies, removes all fossil fuel subsidy, removes any fossil fuel subsidies, removes any fossil fuel subsidy, removes fossil fuel subsidies, removes fossil fuel subsidy, removes the fossil fuel subsidies, removes the fossil fuel subsidy, removing all fossil fuel subsidies, removing all fossil fuel subsidy, removing any fossil fuel subsidies, removing any fossil fuel subsidy, removing fossil fuel subsidy, removing the fossil fuel subsidies, removing the fossil fuel subsidy, the fossil fuel subsidies are eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidies are ended, the fossil fuel subsidies are removed, the fossil fuel subsidies phase-out, the fossil fuel subsidies should be eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidies will be eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidies will be removed, the fossil fuel subsidy are eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidy are ended, the fossil fuel subsidy are removed, the fossil fuel subsidy phase-out, the fossil fuel subsidy should be eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidy will be eliminated, the fossil fuel subsidy will be removed</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">The removal of fossil-fuel subsidies can be by removing the production subsidies, which are tax breaks or direct payments that reduce the cost of producing coal, oil or gas or removing consumption subsidies, which cut fuel prices for the end user, such as by fixing the price at the petrol pump so that it is less than the market rate.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">The removal of a subsidy to fossil fuel companies.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1316 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1316">
